    "issue_alignment": "The public issue describes an overflow condition while processing an ill-formed CGATS file. In this source revision, InStringSymbol() reads a quoted string with while (it8->ch != sng) and only breaks on '\\n' or '\\r'; an unterminated string that runs into the end of the input leaves it8->ch == 0 (EOF marker returned by NextCh for the in-memory stream), which matches none of the exit conditions. The loop therefore never terminates, repeatedly calling StringAppend() with the NUL EOF character. Each growth does s->max *= 10; cmsInt32Number eventually overflows, AllocChunk() yields an undersized or NULL buffer, and memcpy(new_ptr, s->begin, s->len) copies the unbounded s->len bytes into it, corrupting the heap. The upstream fix (commit 32d19328855d 'fix an overflow condition / on ill-formed CGATS file') adds || it8->ch == 0 to the loop break condition."
